# Public functions whose BODY answers a sentinel, per module:
#
#     <module> <failure> <absence>
#
# `failure` answers a raw syscall result - a negative errno - and is
# what `Result` is for. `absence` answers -1 for "not found", which is
# not a failure at all and wants `Option`. `docs/error-model.md`
# ERR-REC-3 draws that line; this file is the first artifact to count
# the two separately, because counting them as one number made the
# migration's size a number nobody could act on.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-30, AND THE METRIC CHANGED UNDER IT. The count
# rose from 13 to 38, and no line of stdlib/ moved. What moved is that
# the census stopped reading DOC-COMMENTS and started reading BODIES.
# `tests/compat/verify-compat.py`'s `sentinel_census` carries the full
# reasoning; the four findings that forced it:
#
#   * THE OLD METRIC REWARDED SILENCE. `netListen` forwards
#     `__syscall3` and hands back a raw fd-or-negative-errno. It was
#     UNCOUNTED, because nobody had written the sentence. Writing the
#     house line above it would have taken stdlib/Sys.ax from 3 to 4
#     and failed `check-compat.sh` for a commit that changed no
#     contract. A gate that goes red when you DOCUMENT an existing
#     sentinel is a gate asking you not to.
#
#   * IT UNDERCOUNTED BY ROUGHLY FOUR TIMES. 13 over 7 modules by
#     prose; 38 over 7 by body. stdlib/Sys.ax alone goes 3 -> 26,
#     because almost every `net*` and `sys*` call forwards a syscall
#     result and almost none of them says so in the house phrasing.
#
#   * ONE OF ITS SIX PATTERNS MATCHED NOTHING. `answers 0, or` appears
#     nowhere in stdlib/ - the tree writes "Answers" - so the only
#     0-sentinel arm was dead.
#
#   * IT COUNTED A CONSTANT. `sysRandomNum` is
#     `(pub fn (sysRandomNum) 33554932)`, the getentropy SYSCALL
#     NUMBER, with no bad path. The comment walk climbed a `; ---`
#     banner into prose describing getentropy's `0 or -errno` contract
#     twelve lines above. That was the whole of this file's old
#     `Sys/Platform.darwin.ax 1`, and the error had already been
#     inherited by `docs/error-model.md`, which named it as one of five
#     failures. The real entropy call, `sysRandomBytes`, was ported
#     long ago and answers `(Result Int Error)`.
#
# THE DIRECTION RULE IS UNCHANGED AND NOW APPLIES PER KIND: neither
# number may rise for a module. Porting a `failure` to `Result` lowers
# the first; porting an `absence` to `Option` lowers the second. Both
# are checked, which the old file could not do - it had a `Result` skip
# and no `Option` skip, so an in-place port of `strFindByte` to
# `(Option Int)` would have left its line exactly where it was, which
# is the regression the `Result` skip existed to prevent.
#
# WHAT A READER WATCHING THESE NUMBERS SHOULD KNOW.
#
# The nine `absence` rows are NOT `Result` debt and two of them cannot
# become `Result` at all: `stdlib/Str.ax` cannot import `Err`, because
# `Err` imports `Str`. Nor is `Option` free - measured 2026-08-30 over
# 20,000,000 calls at `--opt 2`, a `-1` return costs 1.4 ns and a
# `(Some v)` costs 10.4 ns, 7.4x, because the block is allocated,
# stored, matched and released. The arena bump moves ZERO bytes for
# that loop - the block is recycled through its size class - so a
# bytes-only measurement reports `Option` as free and is wrong. The
# cost is instructions. `strFindByte` has 62 call sites on the
# compiler's own scanning path.
#
# The `failure` rows are the migration proper, and were 29 with 26 of
# them in one module. None is free: `netSocketTcp` has 17 call sites,
# seven of which never test the result at all, which is the reason the
# migration exists rather than an argument against it.
#
# WHAT THIS NUMBER STILL DOES NOT REACH, stated rather than left to be
# discovered: the literal-`0` sentinel (`vecGet`, `vecPop`, `vecLast`,
# `strByte`, `jsonGet`, `jsonArrGet`); 114 public MACROS, among them
# `println`, whose value is `writeStr`'s bytes-or-errno Int with 804
# expansions in the tree; and members of `pub extern`, `pub trait` and
# `effect` declarations. About 21% of the public surface is in a form
# `(pub :: ` at column 0 does not match. This is a FLOOR.
#
# PORTED 2026-08-31: `Agent/Tags.ax`'s two (`axsymHexVal`, `axsymPctAt`)
# and `Path.ax`'s two (`pathLastSlash`, `pathExtIndex`) now answer
# `Option Int`. Both modules drop out of this table entirely - the
# census only lists a module with a nonzero count. Zero external
# callers for any of the four (checked by grep over the whole tree
# before porting), so the blast radius was each module's own file;
# `symbols` shows no `#effects=` gained by either, matching the
# existing `Option Int` functions this table already left alone
# (`strFind`), so this is a straight CHANGED row in `compat/BREAKING`,
# not a WIDENED one.
# A DECLARED RISE, 2026-08-31, and the first one this file has carried.
# `stdlib/Tui/Keys.ax` and `stdlib/Tui/Term.ax` arrived with the REPL's
# terminal UI and answer four sentinels between them. They are recorded
# rather than migrated, and the reason is that `Option` is the WRONG
# shape for both:
#
#   * `keyInFill` answers a COUNT of bytes appended, 0 on timeout, -1
#     at end of input and -2 when the buffer cannot take more. That is
#     four outcomes, three of them distinct failures. `Option` collapses
#     -1 and -2 into one `None` and loses the count; `Result` expresses
#     it but allocates, and this runs once per keystroke in a terminal
#     read loop.
#   * `keyCsiParam` answers -1 for a CSI parameter that is absent or
#     empty, and its own comment records why a caller-supplied default
#     is not available: the caller's rule differs by final byte, so
#     `ESC[5~` and `ESC[5D` would become indistinguishable.
#
# The census's direction of travel is unchanged and this is not a
# licence. A sentinel whose meaning is "not found" and nothing else
# still wants `Option`; these two carry more than that.

